storm damage to commercial/institutional roof (heavy-rain roof collapse) | Open - storm-damaged roof | 2026-11-18 (Miami Herald story published 11:36 AM ET, updated 3:16 PM; temple site notice dated 11/18)
Heavy overnight rain (up to 15 in. in Broward County, most in Hollywood) caused a partial collapse of the sanctuary roof at Temple Sinai of Hollywood, 1400 N. 46th Ave, just before 7 AM 11/18; Broward building officials and the Fire Marshal responded; sanctuary waterlogged. Temple site: buildings closed until further notice.
